Apply with git apply -p1 from the extracted beta 4 source root.

--- a/DECK-BETA.md
+++ b/DECK-BETA.md
@@ -1,17 +1,17 @@
-# Deck beta 4 - main-menu controller navigation and button size candidate
+# Deck beta 5 - visible manual room-code entry
 
-Beta 4 clones Together in the original Play button's local UI space, preserves
-its geometry and native button fields, and resets only Together's Unity navigation
-to automatic. It retains beta 3's removal of recursive native hover calls.
-Protocol and assembly version remain 5.1.0.
+Beta 5 separates the Friendlies title, Host, room-code input, keyboard hint,
+Paste/Join buttons, status message and Back into non-overlapping rows. The panel
+is opaque. Select the room-code field with the mouse or controller A, then press
+STEAM+X to type. Paste is optional. Input now permits all 32 characters accepted
+by validation, and the text viewport/caret and native button references are explicit.
+The Together version label stays on one line. Protocol/assembly remain 5.1.0.
 
-The user confirmed beta 3 no longer freezes while hosting, showing a room code,
-or selecting a character. Beta 4 still needs a physical Deck check: move down to
-Together and back up repeatedly, compare its size, then host and select a character.
-A host needs a second player before Confirm becomes available.
+Beta 3's hover recursion correction and beta 4's main-menu navigation and sizing
+corrections are retained. A solo host still needs a second player to confirm.
 
-Compilation, managed stub regressions and compiled-IL checks do not execute the
-native Unity/IL2CPP runtime and cannot establish that the Deck issue is resolved.
+Layout/stub tests and compiled-IL checks do not execute native Unity/IL2CPP.
+Manual typing, controller focus and two-Deck multiplayer still need live testing.
 
